/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
.env
~/.oh-ben-claw/
# Local bench config — may carry ports/tokens; never commit
bench-config.toml
# Runtime SQLite dbs the agent drops in cwd (named after [agent].name)
obc-bench
obc-bench-shm
obc-bench-wal
# Scratch copies of the world-memory db pulled in for offline auditing
_audit/

# Node.js
node_modules/
gui/node_modules/
# tauri-build writes generated schemas and capability manifests here on every
# build. Untracked until 2026-08-14 only because nothing had ever built the GUI.
gui/src-tauri/gen/
npm-debug.log*

# Rust / ESP-IDF build output (any crate, any depth)
**/target/
.embuild/
**/.embuild/

# Editors / IDEs
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user

# Transient bench diagnostic dumps
mesh_status.json
gw40.log

# Python bytecode. New on 2026-08-01: the survey scripts import a shared parser
# (scripts/rust_imports.py) instead of carrying two copies of it, so running one
# now writes scripts/__pycache__/. Untracked-and-unignored is how scratch files
# get swept into commits here.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Commit messages written to a file and passed with `git commit -F`. One was
# swept into a commit by `git add -A` on 2026-08-01, seconds after the scratch
# note below said that is how it happens.
_commitmsg.txt

# Scratch landing area. The Cowork device bridge cannot unlink files, so an
# agent working here moves them aside instead of deleting them. Twice that has
# ended with scratch files committed by accident — they appear as pending
# changes and get swept into a commit. Ignoring the directory removes the
# temptation rather than relying on nobody clicking it.
_to_delete/
